    Vastly simplify JWT setup for common cases (#7189)
    
    Fixes #7034
    
    With this PR, OC administrators only need to change a single line
    (`jwksUrl) in the security config to make common cases (Tobira, LMS)
    work. This does not only benefit admins, but also devs who would
    otherwise have to adjust the security config every time they test
    something with JWT. This is not only annoying, but also error prone. In
    the past, quite a lot of human life time was lost on this non-trivial
    and confusing configuration. I know because I have helped many people
    over the past few years setting up JWT.
    
    You should probably read this PR commit by commit. Basically each commit
    makes the configuration a bit easier.
    
    I don't think this PR is a _perfect_ solution, in that it enables some
    logic to run even if not necessary. But:
    - Most OC installations will actually configure JWT, and then there is
    no useless overhead.
    - Implementing it in a way that admins only have to configure a single
    line, and only then all the machinery is enabled, is _way_ harder than
    this PR.
    - The wasted CPU cycles due to this are minimal, likely swamped by many
    other factors. And if an admin so desires, they can still disable it.
    
    While I hope that this PR gets fully merged, I'm also fine with removing
    some parts, if there are parts that are too controversial to merge
    before the OC 19 branch cut. Every bit helps.
    
    CC @mtneug @joneug
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Not sure how much testing is necessary here. Ideally of course, it is
    tested with a JWT provider like Tobira. I did that and it just works
    after changing this one line.
    
    
